meta {
  name: validation
}

docs {
  Resource-server-side requests against the mock token-validator: health check, `/validate` token introspection, and mock FHIR reads/writes gated by scope and the IG's context rules (every type except Task and Questionnaire needs exactly one context, the recorded counter-party, and graph membership; Task checks `Task.requester` instead). Demonstrates what a real FHIR server is expected to enforce given the claims the AS issues (signature/`iss`/`exp`/`aud`, SMART scopes, `authorization_details`, `organization_reference`).

  Most requests here depend on a token obtained in `auth/` first — see each request's own docs block for which one and which environment variable it reads.
}
